WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.430
In 1986, Nissan opened a
car plant in Sunderland.

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.290
It is now Britain's largest car factory.

3
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.410
It supports a UK workforce
of about 7,000 people.

4
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:17.250
At Redcar, on Teesside, the steelworks
went into liquidation on 2 October 2015.

5
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:24.670
HS2's own 2014 report spoke of the
UK's economic over-reliance on London.

6
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.310
So can one factory or
railway lift a poorer region?

7
00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.650
Do jobs spread fast?

8
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.450
Or does the money all leak to London?

9
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.830
In this mission, you'll trace what
happens when a big plant opens,

10
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:39.070
and when one closes.

11
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.410
Then you'll judge national policies,
from big railways to new local mayors.

12
00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:49.290
Your mission: decide whether one big
investment can help a struggling region catch

13
00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:49.950
up.
